WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:16,950
Hello everybody. This is Dr. Cutters. I wanted to share a short video because I

00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:22,590
will be doing the Zoom this week. The show will be there is multiple questions

00:00:22,590 --> 00:00:27,190
that came in that I want to do a dress. So I put together a little slide

00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:32,430
presentation on this that hopefully this will cover answers for everybody and

00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:37,070
help other people that are may have these same questions. First of all, there was

00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:42,990
somebody that had some diet questions on if I'm on a diet that's low in sugar

00:00:42,990 --> 00:00:51,390
can I eat fruit? So the answer to that is yes and no. So there's there's a

00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:57,710
benefit to certain fruit. Fruit has different nutrients, micro nutrients in it

00:00:57,710 --> 00:01:03,230
that can be extremely beneficial to help fight cancer and and deal with

00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:09,550
different things. Fruit can be gratifying, it satisfies a sweet tooth and such.

00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:13,590
But there are certain fruits that have more carbs and there are certain fruits

00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:20,830
that have fewer carbs. And as this chart points out, the ones on the left have fewer

00:01:20,830 --> 00:01:26,270
carbs, the ones on the right have a greater number of carbs. So we're talking about

00:01:26,270 --> 00:01:32,070
carbohydrates, carbohydrates are what break down to glucose. Glucose is what feeds

00:01:32,230 --> 00:01:39,030
glycolysis and what can fuel cancer. So we don't want to be eating a lot of glucose

00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:47,750
even if you're on a mixed diet where we're still trying to reduce glucose level. So

00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:55,590
people on a ketogenic diet may not eat really any of these fruits except maybe coconuts on this list

00:01:55,590 --> 00:02:04,470
in some lemons but they would probably stay away from even melons as well on a ketogenic diet

00:02:04,470 --> 00:02:09,750
because all these are going to break down fairly rapidly into glucose ultimately.

00:02:11,990 --> 00:02:18,950
Coconut nut so rapidly some of the like lemons and limes won't be very rapidly. There's not a lot

00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:26,070
of fructose in there to break down to glucose. However, on a mixed diet, you still have to be

00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:32,150
aware of any of these. We don't want to be just eating three or four bananas a day or even maybe

00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:39,110
not even eating one banana a day and certainly not grapes and bananas and and a lot of fruit a day

00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:44,550
because you are going to increase your glucose levels by doing that. So you want to use it

00:02:44,630 --> 00:02:51,750
spheridly. So typically the more colorful berries are going to be better for cancer because of the

00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:57,990
antioxidants and the different micro nutrients that are in raspberries and blueberries. Coconut oil

00:02:57,990 --> 00:03:05,030
and coconuts are always good for you on any diet. But there was also a question about coconut oil

00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:14,310
and Alzheimer's just so you know your brain is mainly made up of fats. Coconut oil is a good fat

00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:20,150
for your brain. There was a study that I've cited several times. I don't remember the date of the

00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:25,830
study but it was a few years ago now they were they did what's called an MMI in Victoria which is a

00:03:27,350 --> 00:03:37,030
a assessment test for dementia and early dementia. I can't remember. I think there was 31 patients

00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:44,390
that were assessed to have early dementia and none of them were medicated. All they did with all of

00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:51,270
those patients is put them on three table spoons of coconut oil per day. So they consumed three

00:03:51,270 --> 00:03:59,270
table spoons of coconut oil a day and after one month they reassessed them with that with that test

00:03:59,270 --> 00:04:05,350
and every single one of them improved their score on a test. That was the only change that they made.

00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:13,990
So coconut oil fats are very very very important for your brain so consuming fats is a really important

00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:21,590
thing that you want to continue to do and coconut oil is a good source of a paired oil fat for you.

00:04:23,750 --> 00:04:29,910
As far as you're on a low sugar diet again just try to abide by some reasonableness.

00:04:30,790 --> 00:04:35,190
We don't want to be spiking our glucose levels and certainly you can go out and buy a

00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:41,270
glucometer and measure your glucose to try to keep your glucose levels down. You're fasting

00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:48,790
upon rising when you wake on a bed glucose should be below 90 that's what our goal is.

00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:56,150
So if it's not below 90 then we know we have some work to do with our diet. Now typically most

00:04:56,150 --> 00:05:01,030
my patients are not going to be below the idea of fasting glucose but they first come here.

00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:12,070
And as we start changing their diet and clean out their diet then that will start to drop.

